# ╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  TestcontainerEx — Docker Host Configuration                   ║
# ║  Copy this file to .env and uncomment the right DOCKER_HOST    ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
#
# This file is read by the Dotenv connection strategy ONLY when
# DOCKER_HOST is not already set in your shell environment.
# It allows project-local Docker configuration without modifying
# your shell profile or exporting environment variables.
#
# ── Quick Start ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   1. Copy this file:  cp .env.example .env
#   2. Uncomment the DOCKER_HOST line that matches your runtime
#   3. Run:  mix test
#
# ── Container Engine Host (uncomment ONE) ──────────────────────
# Use $HOME for portability — it expands to your home directory.

# Colima (macOS / Linux lightweight VM runtime)
CONTAINER_ENGINE_HOST=unix://$HOME/.colima/default/docker.sock

# Colima with a named profile (replace "my-profile")
# CONTAINER_ENGINE_HOST=unix://$HOME/.colima/my-profile/docker.sock

# Docker Desktop (macOS)
# CONTAINER_ENGINE_HOST=unix://$HOME/.docker/run/docker.sock

# Docker Desktop (Windows)
# CONTAINER_ENGINE_HOST=unix://$HOME/.docker/desktop/docker.sock

# Docker Engine (Linux default)
# CONTAINER_ENGINE_HOST=unix:///var/run/docker.sock

# Podman rootless socket (Linux)
# CONTAINER_ENGINE_HOST=unix://$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/podman/podman.sock

# Minikube (eval dynamically — sets host, TLS, and cert path)
# eval $(minikube docker-env)

# Remote Docker daemon over TCP (insecure — no TLS)
# CONTAINER_ENGINE_HOST=tcp://192.168.1.100:2375

# Remote Docker daemon over HTTPS (TLS verified)
# CONTAINER_ENGINE_HOST=https://docker.example.com:2376

# Backward compatibility: DOCKER_HOST is also recognized if
# CONTAINER_ENGINE_HOST is not set. Prefer CONTAINER_ENGINE_HOST.

# ── TestcontainerEx Options ──────────────────────────────────────
# These use the TESTCONTAINERS_ prefix and are converted to
# dotted property keys automatically:
#   TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED  →  ryuk.disabled
#   TESTCONTAINERS_PULL_POLICY    →  pull.policy
#   TESTCONTAINERS_REUSE_ENABLE   →  testcontainer_ex.reuse.enable

# Disable the Ryuk reaper container (auto-cleanup of test containers).
# Set to "true" if you don't want containers cleaned up after tests.
# Warning: disabling Ryuk can leave orphaned containers running.
# TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED=false

# Run Ryuk in privileged mode. Needed on SELinux systems or
# rootless Podman where the socket mount is denied.
# TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_CONTAINER_PRIVILEGED=false

# Override the host address used for container connections.
# Useful when the Docker host IP differs from the container gateway.
# TESTCONTAINERS_HOST_OVERRIDE=

# Pull policy: "missing" (default), "always", or "never".
# - "missing" — only pull if the image is not local
# - "always"  — pull on every test run
# - "never"   — never pull, image must exist locally
# TESTCONTAINERS_PULL_POLICY=missing

# Enable container reuse across test runs.
# When "true", containers are not stopped between test runs
# and are reused if their configuration hash matches.
# TESTCONTAINERS_REUSE_ENABLE=false

# ── Debugging ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set the Logger level for TestcontainerEx.
# In dev, the default is :debug; in test, the default is :warning.
# TESTCONTAINERS_LOG_LEVEL=debug
